{
  "id": "m-4.1-extrema",
  "title": "Absolute and local extrema",
  "short": "Extreme values",
  "section": "4.1",
  "minutes": 45,
  "difficulty": 3,
  "objective": "Find absolute and local extreme values, including endpoints and corners.",
  "tags": [
    "exam3"
  ],
  "tabs": [
    {
      "id": "learn",
      "title": "Learn",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "terms",
          "items": [
            [
              "Critical number",
              "An input in the domain where the derivative is zero or undefined."
            ],
            [
              "Extreme value",
              "The output $f(c)$ at a maximizing or minimizing input."
            ],
            [
              "EVT",
              "Continuity on a closed, bounded interval guarantees attainment."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "md": {
            "file": "learn.md"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "formulas",
          "title": "Formulas to know",
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Interior smooth extremum",
              "latex": "\\text{local extremum at differentiable }c\\ \\Rightarrow\\ f^\\prime(c)=0",
              "note": "The converse can fail."
            },
            {
              "label": "Closed-interval candidates",
              "latex": "a,\\quad b,\\quad c\\in(a,b):\\, f^\\prime(c)=0\\text{ or undefined}",
              "note": "Keep c in the domain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "warn",
          "title": "Common errors",
          "md": "Compare outputs, include endpoints, and exclude holes. A zero of $f^\\prime$ outside the interval is irrelevant."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "exam",
          "title": "Written exam practice",
          "md": "Show the candidate table and state the extreme values and where each occurs. Check endpoints even if the prompt gives a derivative."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
